# Doppelgang (X = 2) targets both of Bot2's Ornithopters. In response Bot2 kills one with Lightning Bolt (Mox Ruby). On resolution that target is illegal and is not copied (CR 608.2b), the other still is: two tokens, not four.
# The Ornithopter that was a target and is dead is not copied from the graveyard either.

[Bot1 Deck]
Black Lotus
Mox Emerald
Mox Sapphire
Mox Ruby
Mox Jet
Mox Pearl
Doppelgang
Forest x14

[Bot2 Deck]
Mox Ruby
Lightning Bolt
Ornithopter
Ornithopter
Forest x16

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mox Emerald.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Jet.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Black Lotus.Cast
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Emerald.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Jet.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Black Lotus.Activate(Color: White)
Bot1.Hand.Doppelgang.Cast(X: 2)
Bot1.Target(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1; Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Lightning Bolt.Cast(Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1)
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass

[Expect]
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#1.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#2.Power = 0
Bot1.Battlefield.Ornithopter#3 = (absent)
Bot2.Battlefield.Ornithopter.Power = 0
Bot2.Graveyard = Ornithopter; Lightning Bolt
